+/*
+ * HEVC CABAC context table (928 bytes) for the Hi3798MV100 VDM.
+ *
+ * The decoder reads the table through picture-message word D25. For each of the
+ * 464 hardware CABAC contexts it holds the byte pair (m, n) of the
+ * initialisation process of ITU-T Rec. H.265 section 9.3.1.1 (m = 5 *
+ * slopeIdx - 45, n = 8 * offsetIdx - 16, slopeIdx/offsetIdx being the nibbles
+ * of the spec initValue); the hardware derives the running (pStateIdx, valMps)
+ * from the slice QP itself, so no QP-expanded image is needed. Contexts are
+ * stored per slice type: 144 entries for I slices followed by two 160-entry
+ * blocks for the inter slice types; contexts the hardware does not use carry
+ * the (0, 0) pair. Two contexts pack into one word in little-endian byte order
+ * (m0, n0, m1, n1).
